<title>FRANCE: Alcatel sets 3-firm Thomson-CSF bid - paper.</title>
<headline>Alcatel sets 3-firm Thomson-CSF bid - paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcatel Alsthom has found two French partners in state-owned Aerospatiale and Dassault to prepare a bid for state-controlled electronics firm Thomson-CSF and is waiting to hear the government's terms for privatisation of the latter, daily Les Echos said on Monday.</p>
<p>Les Echos said the involvement of Aerospatiale and Dassault, themselves due to merge, would concern assets only and could involve Dassault parting with its Dassault Electronique unit, while Aerospatiale would contribute its missile and satellite businesses.</p>
<p>The government is due to announce soon how it plans to privatise Thomson-CSF after scrapping its first attempt to sell it off by trade sale late last year.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
